# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows as well as Linux/macOS, and CRLF endings
# have broken CI twice: a CRLF shebang makes a shell script unrunnable on the
# Unix runners, and Vite/esbuild fails to parse a JS module whose hashbang line
# ends in \r. Pin the formats where CRLF is actively harmful.

# Shell scripts are executed directly by the Unix runners.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Parsed by esbuild/Vite, which chokes on a CRLF hashbang.
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf

# Generated — LF keeps regeneration a no-op instead of a whole-file diff.
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf
package-lock.json text eol=lf
